# Configuration for forge-cloud. Copy to /etc/relayforge.env, chmod 600.
#
# Every line here is optional. With none of it set, the control plane runs with
# billing off and every workspace on the Free plan — which is a supported
# deployment, not a degraded one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- billing
#
# Billing stays off unless STRIPE_SECRET_KEY is set. A restricted key with
# Checkout Sessions (write) and Billing Portal (write) is enough; it does not
# need full account access.
#STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_...

# From the webhook endpoint's page in the Stripe dashboard.
#
# Load-bearing: with this empty, *every* webhook is refused. An unset secret is
# never treated as "skip the signature check" — that mistake would let anyone
# who can reach the endpoint upgrade themselves to Team.
#STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...

# The recurring price ids the plans map to. A price the deployment has not been
# told about resolves to Free rather than to a guess.
#STRIPE_PRICE_PRO=price_...
#STRIPE_PRICE_TEAM=price_...

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ notes
#
# The signing key is *not* here. It lives in /var/lib/relayforge/forge-cloud.key,
# created 0600 on first start and reused. Putting it in an env file would mean a
# key in a backup, in a config-management repository, and in the output of
# `systemctl show`.
